# Normalize line endings across the polyglot, multi-OS fleet (Rust/Python/TS).
* text=auto eol=lf
*.png binary
*.pdf binary
*.jpg binary
# The address-literal gate (scripts/address-literals.mjs) skips a file with a NUL byte only when a line here declares it binary.
# Canonical CBOR batches are binary (NUL/control bytes); never eol-normalize them,
# so a pinned sha256 survives commit (the Shōgen s3-binance batch, archived at step 7 of ROADMAP.md, held one)
# deterministically instead of relying on git's content auto-detection (Lot I-a).
*.cbor binary
# OpenTimestamps proofs (served byte-identical under apps/site/public/bell/anchors/, pinned by
# test/bell-anchors.test.ts) and the self-hosted OFL fonts: binary, never eol-normalized, same reason
# as the CBOR batches above (Lot SITE-CHARTE-C).
*.ots binary
*.ttf binary
